    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7857": {
      "title": "University of Hartford Employment Site",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Mail/Print Services Clerk Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Mail/Print Services Clerk Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Mail/Print Services Clerk FLSA Classification NE Reports to Manager, Mail and Print Services Salary Range I1 Weeks Per Year 40 (10 month, academic year) Work Week 35 hours Position Summary Assumes responsibility for operating various types of digital equipment to produce printed goods on various types of media. Also assumes responsibility for providing quality customer service as well as mail and package processing and distribution assistance to all visitors to the Mail Services window in compliance with U.S. Postal Service regulations as well as institutional policies and procedures. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range $17.50 to $19.50 per hour Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Mail Services Provides customer service at the Mail Services window to all students, faculty and staff. Provides guidance and assistance to faculty, staff and students regarding postage charges, mail processes and the internal distribution of materials. Processes and distributes U.S. Postal Service, UPS packages and other parcels for faculty, staff and students. Oversees the accurate and timely processing and tracking of charge backs to departments for metered mail. Unloads, sorts, weighs and meters campus mail and packages. Performs bulk and second-class mailings. Prepares outgoing campus mail and packages for the U.S. Postal Service. Signs receipt for University Express mail. Manages multiple competing priorities under established time constraints. Bundles and arranges mail and packages for University deliveries. Sorts and distributes mail and packages in the department of Mail Services. Meters outgoing mail. As needed, delivers and collects mail, tubs and packages from designated U.S. Post Office, including but not limited to, registered, express, certified and insured packages. Signs for all “accountable” mail, as an authorized University of Hartford Mail Services representative. Loads and unloads trucks with sorted mail. Supplies trays to the U.S. Post Office; delivers permit and bulk mail to the U.S. Post Office. Deposits checks for stamps and picks up stamps at the U.S. Post Office. Assists in other mailroom duties to ensure efficient operations and quality customer service to the University community. Print Services Operates digital equipment including, but not limited to, black and white and color digital presses, cutters, stitchers, sign makers, engravers and laminators to produce signage, nameplates, t-shirts, promotional materials, wide format posters, banners and other high end materials based on client needs. Compiles and inputs job submission data into associated websites and/or systems, complying with data integrity standards as well as other related University policies and procedures. Reviews and verifies all appropriate backup documentation is complete. Assists the Print Services department with signage and promotional items as necessary and/or appropriate. Performs a variety of duties to meet the accurate and timely delivery of materials as well as processing and reconciliation of invoices. Orders and maintains adequate supply levels for routine maintenance. Assists with purchasing materials including, but not limited to supplies, and repair of printers or other digital machines to support the effective operations of the department. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1222P Working Conditions Stockroom or warehouse High noise environment. Requires extensive safety training and/or protective devices. Regular exposure to chemicals, solvents. Work with poor ventilation or with regular exposure to odors. Requires travel, excluding overnight stays. Regular exposure to moving machinery and/or vehicles. Education High School Diploma or GED required. Physical Effort Typically standing and/or walking. Typically pushing and/or pulling. Intermittently sitting, standing, stooping. Moderate lifting or carrying 26 -50 lbs. Requires handling by seizing, holding, grasping, or turning hands, but without finger dexterity. Requires repeated reaching by extending hand(s) and/or arm(s) in any direction. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Valid US driver’s license required. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7856 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7877": {
      "title": "University of Hartford Employment Site",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Manager of Student Services and Evaluation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Manager of Student Services and Evaluation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Manager of Student Services and Evaluation FLSA Classification NE Reports to Assistant Director, Undergraduate Academic Services and Enrollment Compliance Salary Range G1 Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum) Position Summary Assumes responsibility for the support of student academic progress through the Office of the Registrar, primarily through technical and functional use the University’s databases of record. Responsible for updating student records, performing degree evaluations, and awarding of student degrees in assigned college. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range $20 to $21.50 per hour Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Manages student academic progress in Degree Works. Supports the Assistant Registrar in their work managing Degree Works, including assisting with upgrades, testing, data reporting and training. Also collaborates with the Assistant Registrar in identifying areas for improvement for services within the scope of responsibility, which may include new approaches and processes that help promote efficiencies for the Office of the Registrar and University. Serves as a liaison between students and department heads to resolve academic discrepancies, deficiencies in student progress, potential corrective measures and other academic issues as necessary and/or appropriate. Evaluates student academic records. Updates transfer credits into Banner, per college determination. Reviews and/or updates records and related student information used for enrollment, academic statistics, programs and/or scholarship. Assists in the development and implementation of procedures and forms regarding students. Manages multiple priorities under established time constraints. Handles highly sensitive information with confidentiality and tact. Establishes, cultivates and maintains effective working relationships with various internal and external constituencies. Supports Registrar personnel as needed, in one or more of the following areas, scheduling, commencement, Acalog, academic reporting. Maintains departmental files that are accurate and in compliance with record keeping policies. Also files student academic program data to ensure the integrity of the database in compliance with established policies as well as data integrity standards. Represents the Office of the Registrar on committees as necessary and appropriate. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1224P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Education Bachelor’s Degree required. Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Light lifting or carrying 25 lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7860 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue West Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
